# Performance Benchmarking & Profiling Practitioner

**Domain:** Testing / Performance Engineering  
**Standard:** Criterion.rs (Rust) / benchmark.js & Tinybench (Node.js) / pytest-benchmark (Python)

## Overview
Statistically rigorous performance benchmarking, warmup executions, regression detection, and flamegraph profiling. Prevents performance regressions before code hits production.

## Core Rules & Invariants
1. **Warmup Runs Mandatory:** Always execute warmup cycles before taking samples to eliminate JIT compilation or cache coldness artifacts.
2. **Statistical Significance:** Ensure p-value < 0.05 confidence intervals; never declare a regression based on single-run variance.
3. **Isolated Environments:** Benchmarks must run in CPU-pinned or quiet test environments with zero concurrent test worker contention.
4. **Fail on Regression:** Automated CI quality gates must reject any mutation causing statistically significant regressions > 5%.

## Criterion.rs Canonical Pattern (Rust)
```rust
use criterion::{black_box, criterion_group, criterion_main, Criterion};

pub fn benchmark_hashing(c: &mut Criterion) {
    let mut group = c.benchmark_group("sha256_embeddings");
    group.warm_up_time(std::time::Duration::from_millis(500));
    group.measurement_time(std::time::Duration::from_secs(3));
    group.sample_size(100);

    group.bench_function("int8_cosine_similarity", |b| {
        b.iter(|| compute_int8_embedding(black_box("benchmark payload")))
    });
    group.finish();
}

criterion_group!(benches, benchmark_hashing);
criterion_main!(benches);
```

## Node.js Tinybench Pattern (TypeScript)
```typescript
import { Bench } from 'tinybench';

const bench = new Bench({ time: 100, warmupTime: 50 });
bench
  .add('oxc_ast_scan', () => {
    scanAstInvariants(sampleSource);
  })
  .add('regex_baseline', () => {
    regexScan(sampleSource);
  });

await bench.run();
console.table(bench.table());
```
